# Installation

## Requirements

To build Graph Switching you need:

- a C compiler with C99 support, such as GCC or Clang;
- `make`; and
- standard C library headers.

The `install` target also uses a POSIX-style `install` command. nauty and
Traces are optional; they are useful for converting and canonically
labelling the generated graphs but are not build dependencies.

## Build

From the repository root, run:

```sh
make
```

This creates five executables in the repository root:

```text
graphswitching
gen_all_srgs
gen_all_srgs_64vts
gen_all_srgs_wqh6
gen_all_srgs_wqh_generic
```

To compile with a different compiler or optimization level:

```sh
make clean
make CC=clang CFLAGS="-O2"
```

`make check` builds every executable and verifies that `graphswitching`
produces the same adjacency-matrix output as the original generic program
for the included test graph.

## Install

The default installation prefix is `/usr/local`:

```sh
sudo make install
```

Choose another prefix if desired:

```sh
make install PREFIX="$HOME/.local"
```

For package creation, `DESTDIR` is supported:

```sh
make install DESTDIR=/tmp/graphswitching-package PREFIX=/usr
```

Remove installed executables with the same prefix:

```sh
sudo make uninstall
```

## Configure the specialized programs

The graph order is compiled into these three programs:

- `code/gen_all_srgs.c`
- `code/gen_all_srgs_64vts.c`
- `code/gen_all_srgs_wqh6.c`

Edit the `#define VTS` near the top of the desired file, then rebuild its
target. For example:

```sh
make gen_all_srgs_wqh6
```

For `gen_all_srgs_64vts`, `VTS` must fit in the bit width of `INTT`; consult
the source comments before changing either definition.

The recommended `graphswitching` tool and the original generic WQH program
accept the graph order and part size at run time:

```sh
./graphswitching n p < adjacency-matrix.txt
```

They support `n <= 448` and `p <= 8`. The original limits remain in
`code/gen_all_srgs_wqh_generic.c`; the new interface exposes its limits in
`include/graphswitching.h`.

## Clean the build

Remove all generated executables:

```sh
make clean
```
